# Configure WhatsApp

Loom supports WhatsApp configuration at org scope and user-linking flows.

## 1. Set platform client defaults (optional)

```bash
export LOOM_SERVER_WHATSAPP_BASE_URL="https://graph.facebook.com/v21.0"
export LOOM_SERVER_WHATSAPP_TIMEOUT_SECS="30"
```

## 2. Configure org-level WhatsApp credentials

Use web UI routes:

- `/settings/orgs/:orgId/whatsapp`
- `/settings/orgs/:orgId/whatsapp/groups`

Or API routes:

- `POST /api/orgs/{org_id}/whatsapp/config`
- `GET /api/orgs/{org_id}/whatsapp/config`
- `DELETE /api/orgs/{org_id}/whatsapp/config`

## 3. Configure webhook in Meta

Set callback URL:

```text
https://loom.example.com/api/whatsapp/webhook
```

Verification and delivery routes:

- `GET /api/whatsapp/webhook` (challenge verification)
- `POST /api/whatsapp/webhook` (message delivery)

## 4. Link user accounts to WhatsApp identity

User self-service routes:

- `POST /api/users/me/whatsapp/link`
- `POST /api/users/me/whatsapp/verify`
- `DELETE /api/users/me/whatsapp/unlink`

## 5. Validate group routing

Group management routes:

- `GET /api/orgs/{org_id}/whatsapp/groups`
- `POST /api/orgs/{org_id}/whatsapp/groups`
- `DELETE /api/orgs/{org_id}/whatsapp/groups/{group_id}`

Conversation move route:

- `POST /api/orgs/{org_id}/whatsapp/conversations/{conversation_id}/move`

<Callout variant="warning" title="Secret handling">
	Store WhatsApp access credentials as secrets and rotate them periodically.
</Callout>
